  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The threshold wavelength for photoelectric emission from a material is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8728;</mo></mover></math>. Photoelectrons will be emitted, when this material is illuminated with monochromatic radiation from a</p><p>A.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>75</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math> infra-red lamp</p><p>B.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math> infra-red lamp</p><p>C.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>75</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math> ultra-violet lamp</p><p>D.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math> ultra-violet lamp</p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "B and C only",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "A and D only",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "C only",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "C and D only",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given here, threshold wavelength&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#197;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>550</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math></p><p>For photoelectric emission,&nbsp;the wavelength of the light should be less than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>550</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>.</p><p>Wavelength of infrared radiation&nbsp;extends from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>700</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>&nbsp;and that of ultraviolet radiation is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>.</p><p>Since, UV light has less wavelength than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>550</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>, so only UV would be able to emit photoelectrons.</p>"
  }
